1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,632
Welcome to the Refraction Studio training video from QuakeLogic.

2
00:00:04,632 --> 00:00:13,825
In about six minutes you will take a set of seismic refraction shot records to a velocity model, Vs30 and a finished report.

3
00:00:16,525 --> 00:00:19,503
Refraction Studio opens on the start page.

4
00:00:19,503 --> 00:00:25,103
Start a new project, open one, import a survey, or explore the built-in sample:

5
00:00:25,103 --> 00:00:27,018
a complete P and SH survey.

6
00:00:27,018 --> 00:00:32,922
Everything runs on your own computer, with no account and no activation.

7
00:00:35,622 --> 00:00:38,194
Start a new project and describe the site.

8
00:00:38,194 --> 00:00:42,173
These details appear on the report cover and in the audit record.

9
00:00:42,173 --> 00:00:49,255
The workflow on the left takes you through every step, and each step shows its status.

10
00:00:49,555 --> 00:00:55,129
On the Import page, choose files or a whole folder of SEG-2 or SEG-Y records.

11
00:00:55,129 --> 00:00:58,676
Every file is inspected before anything is added:

12
00:00:58,676 --> 00:01:05,629
the format, the traces, the sample interval and the source position from the headers.

13
00:01:05,929 --> 00:01:08,314
Validation lists anything unusual.

14
00:01:08,314 --> 00:01:13,856
Here channel 30 of one shot is flat, so its geophone was probably disconnected.

15
00:01:13,856 --> 00:01:15,890
Nothing is repaired silently:

16
00:01:15,890 --> 00:01:19,047
tick the correction you approve, then import.

17
00:01:19,047 --> 00:01:23,986
The original files are stored unchanged inside the project.

18
00:01:26,686 --> 00:01:28,289
Geometry shows the line:

19
00:01:28,289 --> 00:01:31,361
geophones, shot points and the ground profile.

20
00:01:31,361 --> 00:01:36,503
Positions and elevations recorded in the file headers are used automatically.

21
00:01:36,503 --> 00:01:43,513
You can edit the spread, the channel roles and the shots, or paste a surveyed ground profile.

22
00:01:43,813 --> 00:01:46,386
The Waveforms page shows each shot gather.

23
00:01:46,386 --> 00:01:52,878
Hover over a trace for its details, zoom with the mouse wheel, and step through the shots with the arrows.

24
00:01:52,878 --> 00:01:57,946
The amplitude spectrum helps you choose filters.

25
00:01:58,246 --> 00:02:04,036
Processing is a list of steps applied to copies of the traces; the raw data never change.

26
00:02:04,036 --> 00:02:10,477
Remove the DC offset and, if surface waves obscure the first breaks, add a causal high-pass filter.

27
00:02:10,477 --> 00:02:14,660
Every step can be reordered, switched off or undone.

28
00:02:17,360 --> 00:02:20,324
On the P picks page, press Pick automatically.

29
00:02:20,324 --> 00:02:28,660
Refraction Studio picks the first arrival on every trace and gives each pick a confidence, with its reasons.

30
00:02:28,960 --> 00:02:32,412
Accept the high-confidence picks, then review the rest.

31
00:02:32,412 --> 00:02:38,311
Click a trace to place or move a pick, nudge it with the arrow keys and press Enter to accept.

32
00:02:38,311 --> 00:02:44,195
Manual picks are never overwritten, and the travel-time plot updates as you work.

33
00:02:46,895 --> 00:02:52,657
On the Velocity model page, choose the number of layers and press Suggest layer assignment.

34
00:02:52,657 --> 00:02:57,659
Check the crossovers on the travel-time plot, then apply the delay-time method.

35
00:02:57,659 --> 00:03:04,795
The layered model gives each layer's velocity and the depth to the refractor under every geophone.

36
00:03:05,095 --> 00:03:07,658
For a gradational model, run tomography.

37
00:03:07,658 --> 00:03:11,824
The inversion stops when the misfit matches the pick uncertainty.

38
00:03:11,824 --> 00:03:18,456
Cells below the depth of investigation are hatched, because the data do not constrain them.

39
00:03:21,156 --> 00:03:25,896
Quality control checks the picks, the timing, the geometry and the models.

40
00:03:25,896 --> 00:03:31,662
Each finding explains what was found and what to check; double-click it to open the trace.

41
00:03:31,662 --> 00:03:36,305
The summary is an aid to review, not a compliance statement.

42
00:03:36,605 --> 00:03:38,526
Save the project with Ctrl+S.

43
00:03:38,526 --> 00:03:49,458
The project file holds the raw data, every processing step and pick, and the complete history, so the analysis can be reproduced and every change undone.

44
00:03:52,158 --> 00:03:55,472
The built-in sample has a P line and an SH line.

45
00:03:55,472 --> 00:04:00,996
SH shots are recorded with a shear beam struck from the left and from the right.

46
00:04:00,996 --> 00:04:11,118
Refraction Studio combines each pair so that shear energy adds and P energy cancels, and picks the SH arrivals with a dedicated picker.

47
00:04:11,418 --> 00:04:15,387
Engineering combines the shear-wave and P-wave models:

48
00:04:15,387 --> 00:04:22,223
Vs30, average velocities over chosen depth intervals, Poisson's ratio and the elastic moduli.

49
00:04:22,223 --> 00:04:31,770
Vs30 is reported only where the model reaches 30 m unless you choose to extrapolate, and estimates are always labelled.

50
00:04:32,070 --> 00:04:37,021
Results summarises every line and compares analysis scenarios.

51
00:04:37,021 --> 00:04:47,722
Export the tables to Excel or CSV, the figures as PNG, SVG or PDF, and an audit record of the methods, settings and history.

52
00:04:50,422 --> 00:04:58,106
On the Report page, enter the report details and conclusions, choose the sections and add your company branding.

53
00:04:58,106 --> 00:05:07,522
Generate PDF report writes the complete technical report.

54
00:05:07,822 --> 00:05:20,859
The report covers the project and the survey configuration, shot gathers, travel-time curves, the layered and tomographic models, Vs30, the engineering parameters, quality control and processing notes,

55
00:05:20,859 --> 00:05:25,486
with the software version and settings for reproducibility.

56
00:05:28,186 --> 00:05:30,136
Help is always one key away.

57
00:05:30,136 --> 00:05:36,751
Press Ctrl+K to find any command, F1 for help on the current page, or choose Explain this step.

58
00:05:36,751 --> 00:05:45,419
Guided mode shows a short guidance box on each page; Expert mode hides it.

59
00:05:45,719 --> 00:05:47,874
That is the complete workflow.

60
00:05:47,874 --> 00:05:57,008
Read the field guide before your first survey, and contact QuakeLogic support at any time at support@quakelogic.net.
